  "name": "Stone lantern (ishi-doro): Kasuga, square standing and small placed types, 3 heights",
  "importance": "standard",
  "tiers": [
   2,
   3
  ],
  "abandoned_state": "Stone lanterns shed their top parts in quakes: 1 in 6 has its hoju or kasa on the ground beside it; the rest are dark, lichen-streaked and mossy on the roof.",
  "placement_rule": "In mirrored pairs at the torii and the hall steps; rows of 4-20 on town approaches (landmark only); single oki-doro in courtyard gardens.",
